**7. Builder, ring, and solver consumption.** The compiler now defaults its CLI to source-complete support, keeps raw D1 as an explicitly conditional diagnostic, and applies `builder_fix.fix_text` at every emission. That ensures a support re-emission cannot silently restore the old transcendental coefficient field and its OOM behavior. The final ring is

    Q[y,x,h_ba,Ai_ba,Bi_ba,c], order (lp(1),dp(N+1)),

with the y-first block, so lead(h)=y^K independently of the x-degrees. Monic `division()` returns a unit matrix equal to one. Extraction writes all coefficient rows. The existing level cap is amply exhaustive: deg_y P=eK, deg_y Q=qK, so deg_y J≤(e+q)K−1 and its h-adic level is at most e+q−1. Adding x powers never increases that y-degree bound. The runtime gates check monicity, division units, a nonzero target coefficient polynomial, completion marker, and agreement between declared and actual row count. A header-only file, timeout, or `halt 1` is not a valid empty ideal or a full generator set.

The native inherited builder uses low polynomial Q first in its Jacobian, whereas `jacobian_check.py` presents high polynomial P first. This is the harmless but explicit map c_native=−c_(P,Q), T_native=−T_(P,Q); Tc−1 maps to itself. The source-support and UNIT statements are invariant under this invertible sign map. Merely matching variable names would not establish it.

For an expanded direct representation, the polynomial coefficient ideal of J−cx^ell in ordinary x,y equals the h-adic coefficient ideal. Over the parameter ring, monicity makes {y^a h^j:0≤a<K,j≥0} a triangular basis over Q[parameters,x] with diagonal ones. Both coefficient lists are finite polynomial combinations of the other. This proves equality of coefficient ideals before and after adjoining Tc−1, including nonreduced parameter fibres. A direct emitter therefore changes the generator list, not the chart or the support obligation. The original control generators were preserved; alternatives run in separate paths.

For the full re-solves, an exact graph extension also avoids expanding high powers of h. At each Horner stage for P and Q, introduce only needed coefficient variables U and impose U−coefficient(previous stage·h+α_i or β_i)=0; use β1=0. All auxiliary definitions are monic and triangular in stage order. Quotienting by them identifies the extended ring with the original parameter ring. The final ordinary x,y coefficients of J(Q,P)−cx^ell then generate precisely the original chart ideal under this isomorphism. Adjoining Tc−1 commutes with the isomorphism. No branch, denominator, or parameter specialization is involved. The circuit auxiliary counts are listed separately from intrinsic chart counts; the solver ring also adds one inverse variable. Twenty-two exact-Q differential controls pass. An independent formal reconstruction checks every graph and Jacobian row, and inverse-maps every actual msolve input polynomial, with no dropped term or row.

