UNIT custody includes exact input and row selection, coefficient field and variable map, inverse equation, solver identity, return code and valid output envelope. `msolve_chart.py` round-trips the rename and uses the pinned `msolveio` emitter. A subset UNIT is enough only if every selected generator is actually a generator of the declared completed presentation (including a validated graph extension). A cap, a prefix PARAMETER specialization, or a mismatched metadata/rows pair is not such a subset.

A modular UNIT is only a signal. In particular the installed msolve 0.6.5/0.10.1 behavior can return a first-prime `[1]` even when invoked in characteristic zero; a zero-characteristic label alone is not an exact rational membership certificate. The acceptance rule is independent exact-Q confirmation on the identical selected generators, or an explicit rational identity Σ a_i f_i=1 checked in the declared ring. Degree-bounded or timed-out non-UNIT output proves neither nonemptiness nor emptiness. No old timeout, partial extraction, modular result, or solver success string is consumed as theorem (T).

