## FALLACY-v2 Check

The actual D108 kill localizes only at:

```text
c != 0
```

This is nonzero on the charged gauge because `p=pi^2-c` represents a two-simple
root `[1,1]` branch; equivalently, before translation gauge the sourced
condition is the quadratic discriminant `b^2+4c != 0`.  The weakened-gauge
replay localizes at that discriminant and also dies.

No `jet1`, `jet2`, `e0`, `Hc_*`, or outer coefficient is inverted.  The `Q*`
pivots invert only rational constants (`±1` in the charged incidence pivots).
`Zc` and `ZD` are Rabinowitsch variables, not additional nonvanishing
assumptions.  No `sat()` wrapper is used.

No exit-price assertion is made, so no `charge_basis` line is emitted.

