Moh's approximate-root definition on printed p.148 and Theorem 1.1 on p.149 distinguish a polynomial approximate root from arbitrary matching leading terms. Theorem 1.2, printed p.149/PDF page 10, imposes y-degree <K on expansion coefficients and order at least j times the root accuracy. Its hypotheses include a common coherent complete system and the corresponding quasi-approximate root. It does not impose total degree ≤jK. Nor does it state that a y-monic polynomial of degree K has x-degree ≤K−V2. Frozen `order-basis-full-gpt55-20260903.md:38` correctly describes the result as a necessary order lower bound, but the later inventory also imposed caps that do not follow from that lower bound.

