## Result

Both new necessity gaps of the charged (99,66) dossier are **free gauges**.
The chart's simultaneous vanishing of the two constant centres, and the
normalisation `e^{12}`-coefficient `= 1` (equivalently the `h2` `D_2` face
`(pi^3-1)^8`), meet every orbit of the residual affine group that already
fixes the two points at infinity, the two monic top forms, and `J=1`.
The split-branch kills therefore need no extra assumption. Typed:

```text
DISCHARGED[N3]  GAP[TWO-CENTRE-NORMALISATION]   free gauge
                group element: source translations (x,y) |-> (x+c, y+b)
DISCHARGED[N4]  GAP[D1-RECENTRING-SCALE]        free gauge
                group element: eigenbasis 2-torus A_{gamma,delta} with
                gamma^{119} delta^{44}=1, acting by beta |-> beta/(gamma^3 delta)
THEOREM 8.1 residual gaps:  N1, N2, case (A)
```

No kill was re-run: the assigned alternative is the orbit argument, and both
gaps fall in (a). The pivot closed form `|coeff| = 9(99-3n-11i)` is a polynomial
in the Jacobian band indices only; its support is the `B1c` block against the
homogenised top form `A_0 = w^9(w-1)^{24}`, which does not involve `w_0`,
`a_0`, or `beta`. The tame two-point automorphism `(ax+y,(a-1)x+y)` survives
both group elements. No `charge_basis` line: no new exit price is asserted.

The charged dossier's two errors are local to the residual-group computation,
not to the rows. (N3) it treated the translation group as one-dimensional
(`y |-> y-b`); the second generator is `x`-translation, which moves the
`y`-only invariant `w_0-a_0`. (N4) it took the residual torus after placing
the two lines to be `(x,y)|->(s x, s' y)`, which preserves the coordinate
axes rather than `y=0` and `y=x`; the torus that actually preserves those two
lines still has one free parameter after `J=1`, and that parameter sets `beta`.

