## 1. The residual group on the 7,161-chart

### 1.1 Ambient group, from the dossier and Moh

Dossier §2.1: `Gamma` consists of `A in GL_2(k)` acting on `(x,y)`, together
with source translations, target translations, and target scalings
`(F,G) |-> (lambda (F o A), mu (G o A))`. Each element preserves the Keller
condition up to the explicit factor `lambda mu det(A)`, the degrees, and the
characteristic data. Moh p.194 (printed; PDF page 55 of the frozen file)
normalises the two-point leading form
`[(y-ax)^{v_s}(y-bx)^{u_s}]^{n/d_s}` and records the major/minor expansions

```text
(8)  y = a t^{-1} + c_i + higher     (major disc; "choose y so that a=0")
(9)  y = b t^{-1} + e + c_j t + ...  (minor disc; e common)
(10) z = y - b x - e
```

The charged chart is the same two-point normalisation in a different
eigenframe: minor line `y=0`, major line `y=x`,
`P = y^3(y-x)^8`, `in F = P^9`, `in G = P^6`. Proposition 1.2 of the
dossier is a bijection from `k^{7161}` onto that set of monic pairs.

### 1.2 What is already spent, and what remains

Count, after sending the two *points at infinity* to `[1:0]` and `[1:1]`
(the directions of `y=0` and `y=x`):

| piece | dim | spent on |
|---|---:|---|
| `GL_2` | 4 | 2-torus remains (stabiliser of two points of `RP^1`) |
| source translations | 2 | unused in dossier §2.1 |
| `(lambda, mu)` | 2 | monicity of `in F`, `in G` |
| **subtotal after two points + two top forms** | **4** | |
| residual isotropic scaling | 1 | `J_0=1` (factor `s^{-163}`) |
| **residual continuous group on the chart** | **3** | 2 translations + 1 torus |

Target translations `(F,G)|->(F+e_1,G+e_2)` remain available and unused
(dossier §2.2–2.3); they are not needed here.

The 2-torus that preserves *both* eigenlines (not the coordinate axes) is

```text
A_{gamma,delta}(x,y) = (gamma x + (delta-gamma) y,  delta y),
gamma, delta in k^*.
```

It is diagonal in the basis `(1,0)` (along `y=0`) and `(1,1)` (along `y=x`).
`det A = gamma delta`. Pullback of the top form, computed by substituting
into `P` simultaneously:

```text
P o A = gamma^8 delta^3 P.
```

Hence `F o A` has leading form `gamma^{72} delta^{27} P^9` and `G o A` has
leading form `gamma^{48} delta^{18} P^6`. The monic restorers are
`lambda = gamma^{-72} delta^{-27}`, `mu = gamma^{-48} delta^{-18}`, and

```text
J(lambda F o A, mu G o A) = gamma^{-119} delta^{-44} J(F,G).
```

The isotropic slice `gamma=delta=s` recovers the dossier's `s^{-163}`.
The condition `J=1` is the single constraint `gamma^{119} delta^{44}=1`,
leaving a one-parameter torus. Dossier §2.1(iii) instead wrote the
coordinate-axis torus `(x,y)|->(s x, s' y)`, which sends `y=x` to
`y=(s/s')x` and therefore forces `s=s'` as soon as the major line is
required to stay at `y=x`. That is a different 2-torus: it preserves
`y=0` and `x=0`, not `y=0` and `y=x`. After placing the two lines, the
*correct* residual torus is `A_{gamma,delta}`, and `J=1` does not kill it.

### 1.3 Action on the coordinates named by N3 and N4

Write `t=x^{-1}`, `w=y/x`. After the two top forms are fixed, a general
pair in the chart has

```text
major D_2 centre:   y = x + w_0 + pi x^{-1/3} + ...     (w = 1 + w_0 t + pi t^{4/3}+...)
minor centre:       y = a_0 + O(t)                      (w = a_0 t + ...)
h2 D_2 face:        (pi^3 - beta)^8
D_1 recentring:     t=e^9,  w = 1 + alpha e^{12} + Pi e^{13},   alpha^3 = beta.
```

Vieta on `h3=P+H`, with `[y^{10}]P=-8x` and `h_{10}:=[y^{10}]H` constant
(`H in S(10,11)`), is the identity `8 w_0 + 3 a_0 + h_{10} = 0`.

**Translations** `F_new(x,y)=F(x+c,y+b)` (Jacobian 1; leading forms
unchanged, since `P(x+c,y+b)-P` has degree `<=10`, so the chart shape
`h3=P+H` is preserved):

```text
w_0 |-> w_0 + c - b,     a_0 |-> a_0 - b,     h_{10} |-> h_{10} + 11 b - 8 c.
```

The `y`-only slice `c=0` is the one-parameter group of dossier §2.4, with
invariant `w_0-a_0` and with `8w_0+3a_0=-h_{10}` the quantity it can set
to zero. The second generator `c` moves that invariant.

**Torus** `A_{gamma,delta}`, on the slice `w_0=a_0=0` (so both actual
root-lines pass through the origin, which `A` fixes):

```text
w_0 |-> w_0/gamma,     a_0 |-> a_0/delta,     pi |-> pi gamma^{-1} delta^{-1/3},
beta |-> beta/(gamma^3 delta),     alpha |-> alpha/(gamma delta^{1/3}).
```

Zeros of `(w_0,a_0)` are preserved. Near `w=1` one has `t |-> t/delta` and
`w-1 |-> (gamma/delta)(w-1)`, so the `e^{12}` coefficient scales as
stated. Near `w=0` one has `t |-> t/gamma`.

The local stretch `Qc_{r,q} |-> alpha^q Qc_{r,q}` of dossier §3.4 is a
*different* map: it is `K(t,w)|->K(t, 1+alpha(w-1))`, i.e.
`(x,y)|->(x, x+alpha(y-x))`. It preserves `y=x` and moves `y=0`. It is
therefore not an element of the two-point residual group, and cannot by
itself discharge the joint ideal (the dossier's N4 diagnosis of that map
is correct). The eigenbasis torus is the joint-ideal replacement.

## 2. N3: `w_0-a_0` is not a modulus

### 2.1 Transitivity

On the plane `8w_0+3a_0+h_{10}=0` the two translations act faithfully
(`b=c=0` is the only kernel point). The unique solution of
`(w_0+c-b, a_0-b)=(0,0)` is `b=a_0`, `c=a_0-w_0`. Substituting into Vieta
gives `h_{10}^{new}=0` automatically.

Exact model, the intercept-product of the same multiplicities as `h3`:

```text
h3 = (y-a_0)^3 (y-x-w_0)^8.
```

Its degree-11 homogeneous part is exactly `P` for every `(w_0,a_0)`;
`[y^{10}](h3-P)=-8w_0-3a_0`; and

```text
h3(x+(a_0-w_0), y+a_0) = y^3(y-x)^8 = P
```

identically. So both centres, and consequently `h_{10}`, are killed by a
source translation, with the chart shape preserved.

The same transitivity holds in Moh's intermediate frame (major horizontal
`y=kappa`, minor `y=m x+e`, `m!=0`): `y`-translation moves both intercepts,
`x`-translation moves only the minor intercept, and
`(beta,c)=(kappa, (kappa-e)/m)` kills both. The charged probe that
"`a_0 != w_0` is not a translate" is correct for the *one-parameter*
`y`-group and does not constrain the full translation group.

### 2.2 Approximate roots and the tower

The `d`-th approximate root is unique monic of `y`-degree `N/d` with
`deg_y(Q-h^d)<N-N/d`. If `Q'(x,y)=Q(x+c,y+b)` then `h'(x,y)=h(x+c,y+b)`
satisfies the same bound and is monic, so the tower translates. Tschirnhausen
omissions are identities of the approximate root in char 0, not gauges, and
are preserved.

### 2.3 Why the desk-scale probe does not obstruct

Dossier §2.4: expanding at `w=1+w_0 s^3+pi s^4` with all 66 lower `h3`
slots unknown, for `w_0 in {0,1,2,-3}`, yields 45 rows of rank 45 and 21
free — the same counts as at `w_0=0`, with a different, non-diagonal row
set. That is the linearisation of the *un-normalised slice*, not the gauge
orbit. The orbit map translates the whole pair, hence transforms the 21
free coordinates along with `w_0`. Equal rank on every slice is what a
free gauge predicts.

### 2.4 Pivot support, in case one insisted on enlarging the chart

The Jacobian mechanism of dossier §5, below the `A2/A3/B2` onset, is

```text
[t^n] KJ = A_0^3 ( 99 A_0 B_{n-1,w} - (99-3n) B_{n-1} A_{0,w} ),
A_0 = w^9(w-1)^{24} = t^{33} P(t^{-1},w/t)^3,
```

linear in the `B1c_{n-1,*}` block. `A_0` is the homogenised *top form* of
`h2`, independent of `H`, of the `h2` face scale `beta`, and of both
centres. The valuation of `A_0^3 A_{0,w}` at `w=0` is 35, so rows `k<35`
are vacuous, and the `k=35` coefficient is `-9(99-3n)` times
`sum_q (-1)^q B1c_{n-1,q}`. Sequential elimination against the `B1` `D_2`
support and the two outer-`D_1` offset-0 kills reproduces
`|coeff|=9(99-3n-11i)`, which vanishes only if `11|n`, impossible for
`1<=n<=8`. None of `w_0`, `a_0`, `h_{10}` occurs in these rows.

Had `w_0-a_0` been a modulus, the *Jacobian* certificate would therefore
have survived an enlarged chart; the *pole* rows would not, because the
minor expansions of dossier §4.1 start at `y=u t+...` with `a_0=0`. That
counterfactual does not arise: the translation already sets `a_0=0`.

### 2.5 Verdict

`DISCHARGED[N3]`. Group element: `(x,y)|->(x+c,y+b)` with
`(b,c)=(a_0,a_0-w_0)`. Every Keller pair with the two-point leading form
is `Gamma`-equivalent to one with `w_0=a_0=h_{10}=0`. The 45 inner `h3`
rows of the charged chart are the correct necessary rows on that slice.

## 3. N4: `beta` is free for the joint ideal

### 3.1 The missing parameter is the eigenbasis torus

After N3, both actual root-lines pass through the origin, so
`A_{gamma,delta}` is residual. Impose `gamma^{119} delta^{44}=1` to keep
`J=1`. The face scale transforms by `beta |-> beta/(gamma^3 delta)`.
Setting `gamma^3 delta = beta` (i.e. `beta_{new}=1`) together with the
Jacobian constraint is the eliminant

```text
gamma^{13} = beta^{44}.
```

Over algebraically closed `k` of char 0, `beta != 0` (the `D_1` node of
the skeleton exists: `V_2=8`, so the 24 `D_2` roots of `h2` form three
clusters of eight, and `beta=0` would collapse them to `pi=0`), a 13th
root exists. Witness in `k(r)`: `beta=r^{13}`, `gamma=r^{44}`,
`delta=r^{-119}`. Then `alpha = beta^{1/3}` becomes 1, which is the
charged `D_1` recentring `w=1+e^{12}+Pi e^{13}`.

The isotropic leftover `s^{163}=1` only multiplies `beta` by a 163rd root
to the 4th; it is not enough, and is not needed once the non-isotropic
direction is restored.

### 3.2 Action on every row family of the joint ideal

The transformation
`(F,G) |-> (lambda F o A, mu G o A)`
with `lambda,mu` as in §1.2 and `gamma^{119} delta^{44}=1` is an
automorphism of the set of monic pairs with leading forms `P^9`, `P^6`
and `J=1`. Geometric conditions that depend only on those data, on the
two points at infinity, and on the characteristic radii, are preserved as
sets. Explicitly:

| family | action |
|---|---|
| two top forms | restored by `lambda, mu`; `P o A = gamma^8 delta^3 P` |
| Tschirnhausen omissions | identities of `A_d` in char 0; `A_d` intertwines with linear `A` by uniqueness |
| inner `h3` `D_2` face `pi^8` | `pi |-> pi/(gamma delta^{1/3})`; a linear power remains a linear power |
| inner `h2` `D_2` face `(pi^3-beta)^8` | `(pi^3 - beta/(gamma^3 delta))^8`; set `gamma^3 delta=beta` to obtain `(pi^3-1)^8` |
| inner / outer `D_2` unit rows `3r+4q < threshold` | near `w=1`, `(t,w-1)` scales; weights scale uniformly; vanishing below a weight is preserved as a set |
| outer / `h2` `D_1` bands | `alpha |-> alpha/(gamma delta^{1/3})`; `ord_{D_1}` is a characteristic radius, preserved; this is the map whose binomial matrices `M(alpha)` are equivalent of rank `44/73/15/44` and `7` (dossier §3.4), now induced by an actual two-point automorphism rather than by `T_alpha` |
| minor leaders and pole rows | `w=0` is fixed; near `w=0`, `t |-> t/gamma`; branch type (`p=pi^2(pi+3a)` or `p=pi(pi^2-c)`) is preserved; `(u,rho,c)` scale, matching Xu's face gauge `pi |-> lambda pi` (dossier Lemma 7.1 Step 6), which the engine already keeps symbolic |
| Jacobian rows | `J |-> 1` identically, by construction of `lambda, mu, gamma, delta`; every bi-degree coefficient of `J-1` remains zero |
| centres | stay at 0 (§1.3) |

Because the map is an automorphism of the ambient set of pairs, it is a
symmetry of the *joint* ideal, not merely of the `D_1` rank tables. Every
orbit with `beta != 0` meets the slice `beta=1`. The charged presentation
of the `D_1` rows (and of the eight `h2` face slots
`Qc_{4k,24-3k}=(-1)^k binom(8,k)`) is therefore WLOG for the joint
system.

The map `Qc_{r,q}|->alpha^q Qc_{r,q}` remains what the dossier said it
was: a symmetry of the `D_1` block alone. It is not the group element
that discharges N4.

### 3.3 Why the kill need not be re-run with `beta` free

On the slice `beta=1` the engine rows are necessary (dossier §§3–5, with
N4 now supplied by §3.1 rather than assumed). Emptiness of that slice
empties every orbit. Carrying `beta` as a free coordinate would mix the
`r=4` face slot of `K2` into Jacobian bands `n>=5` and would change the
`D_1` binomial matrix; that is a different presentation of an isomorphic
quotient, not a larger scheme. The `Q*`-pivot coefficients
`9(99-3n-11i)` are computed from `A_0` (the top form, independent of
`beta`) and do not see the face until after the `delta=2` death at
stage 4; the `delta=5/2` death is a `G`-pole row. None of this is needed
once the slice is known to be a complete set of representatives.

### 3.4 Verdict

`DISCHARGED[N4]`. Group element: `A_{gamma,delta}` with
`gamma^{13}=beta^{44}` and `delta=beta/gamma^3`, followed by the monic
restorers of §1.2. Every Keller pair with the two-point leading form,
`J=1`, and both centres at 0 is `Gamma`-equivalent to one with
`h2` `D_2` face `(pi^3-1)^8` and `D_1` offset `e^{12}`.

## 4. Dimension check and order of operations

```text
Aff_2 + (lambda,mu)                              8
fix two points at infinity                      -2
monic in F and in G                             -2
J=1                                             -1
(w_0,a_0)=(0,0)                                 -2     N3
beta=1                                          -1     N4
residual continuous moduli                       0
```

Order: (i) `GL_2` sends the two directions to `y=0`, `y=x`; (ii) `lambda,mu`
make the top forms `P^9`, `P^6`; (iii) translations set both intercepts
to 0, so the actual root-lines pass through the origin; (iv) the residual
eigenbasis torus with `J=1` sets `beta=1`. Step (iv) preserves the slice
of step (iii). Finite leftover: 13th roots in `gamma^{13}=beta^{44}`, and
163rd roots of isotropic scaling; both are absorbed over algebraically
closed `k`.

## 5. Control: the tame two-point automorphism

The charged control is `F=a x+y`, `G=(a-1)x+y`, with `J=1` identically,
inverse `x=F-G`, `y=a G-(a-1)F`, and witness slice `(2x+y, x+y)`. Degrees
`(1,1)`: the `s=3` tower, outer `D_1`/`D_2` bands, and `T2,T3` bridge are
`NOT-APPLICABLE`.

Both group elements act as expected:

* source translation: `J` remains 1; the pair stays two linear forms
  (two points at infinity, possibly not through the origin);
* eigenbasis torus: `J` is multiplied by `det A=gamma delta`, restored to 1
  by scaling one factor by `1/det A`; the pair stays two linear forms.

The plumbing that would have to kill a genuine two-point automorphism
therefore still does not kill this one. A two-point automorphism of
degrees `>=6` does not exist (Jung–van der Kulk), so there is no
higher-degree two-point positive control; that limitation is already in
the charged dossier and is unchanged.

## 6. FALLACY-v2

* **Flag/place/series.** The major flag (`D_2`, `D_1`, radii `1/3`, `4/9`,
  residue `y=x`), the principal-minor place (`y=0`, `u_s=3`), and the
  `h2` face scale `beta` are distinct. Translations move affine intercepts
  and do not move points at infinity; the eigenbasis torus scales the two
  eigenlines separately and does not identify them.
* **Floor/attainment.** Theorem 1.2 is not used. The two inner faces are
  rows because the leading forms are fixed and, after N4, the `D_2` face
  of `h2` is a gauge slice, not a new equality theorem.
* **Carrier/attainment.** Nothing is `REPRESENTATIVE` or
  `FULL_ACTUAL_EXIT`. No pair is recomposed.
* **Pole/interior.** No new pole identity. Pole rows of the charged
  engine are consumed as already-promoted necessary rows on the
  gauge-fixed slice.
* **`sat()` wrapping.** None.
* **Raw remainder degree.** None; no new normal form.
* **Variable/ring map.** Declared: `A_{gamma,delta}` as above, monic
  restorers `lambda,mu`, source translations `(x,y)|->(x+c,y+b)`,
  homogenisation `K_Q=t^D Q(t^{-1},w/t)`, field `Q` in the script and `k`
  in the theorem. Name agreement with the engine is not used as evidence.
* **Prime label/derivative.** No derivative is taken except the Jacobian
  determinant of `A` and of the tame control, which is the algebraic
  Jacobian, not a Puiseux `d/dpi`.
* **Merge-free/M-descent; target/arrival index.** Not used.

No exit-price assertion, so **no `charge_basis` line**.

## 7. THEOREM 8.1 after the discharge

The charged statement assumed `N1`--`N4` and that the principal minor
roots split (Lemma 7.1 cases (B) or (C)). N3 and N4 are now supplied by
the residual group of §1, with the two group elements of §§2–3. The
proof of dossier §8 therefore runs without those two hypotheses:

**Theorem 8.1 (conditional).** `k` algebraically closed of char 0.
Let `(F,G) in k[x,y]^2` satisfy `J(F,G) in k^*`, `deg F=99`, `deg G=66`,
with Moh characteristic data `M=(-66,77,97)`, `d=(99,33,11,1)`,
`V=(8,8)` (so `s=3`, `d_s=11`, `v_s=8`, `u_s=3`), and with the principal
minor roots split (case (B) or (C) of Lemma 7.1). Assume `N1` and `N2`.
Then no such pair exists.

Residual gaps, exactly the inherited ones plus the unsplit case:

```text
N1   GAP[MOH-CENSUS-COMPLETENESS]          literature; out of scope
N2   GAP[XU-8(i)-STEP] + GAP[DEN(delta)<=u_s]   literature; out of scope
(A)  unsplit principal-minor configuration     NOT-ADDRESSED
```

`OPEN[EFFECTIVE-T2-T3-BRIDGE]` remains an omission of rows and cannot
rescue a unit ideal. The theorem is still not a statement about
unrestricted degrees `(99,66)` (that needs `N1` and case (A)), nor about
the other census classes, nor about the two-dimensional Jacobian
conjecture.

